======================================================================
OVERALL RESULT
======================================================================

PASS

ESP-LOCAL-001 demonstrated that authority-admissibility recognition can
execute directly on a resource-constrained XIAO ESP32-S3 and gate local
physical command issuance.

The tested endpoint retained local actuator capability while the local
recognition function distinguished admissible requests from tested
requests outside the defined bounds.

The accepted path produced independently witnessed electrical actuator
command activity.

The witnessed denied path produced no observed actuator-command burst.

======================================================================
CLAIM BOUNDARY
======================================================================

ESP-LOCAL-001 is a placement and execution-gating proof.

The incoming request representation in this test was not
cryptographically authenticated as authority issued by an external
provider. The endpoint evaluated a locally defined admissibility
predicate over the received representation.

This test therefore does not, by itself, demonstrate:

- cryptographic attribution to an external provider;
- resistance to forged provider authority;
- replay resistance;
- freshness or expiration enforcement;
- protected endpoint trust-anchor storage;
- secure boot or firmware integrity;
- resistance to endpoint compromise;
- exactly-once physical execution; or
- independent verification of mechanical actuator state.

Those properties require separate evidence.
